.TH tusequence n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tusequence
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBsequenceDiagram\fR block and renders it natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine. A self\-contained 2D renderer in the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR family (like \fBtugantt\fR / \fBtusankey\fR); normally you call \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR / \fBtuflow::toPng\fR, which dispatch here.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tusequence 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tusequence::parse text                      ;# -> sequence model dict
::tclutils::tusequence::toSvg  model ?-width W? ?-height H? ?-fontfile f? ?-scale n?
::tclutils::tusequence::toPng  model ?...?              ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tusequence::writeSvg model file ?...?
::tclutils::tusequence::writePng model file ?...?
.CE
.PP
\fB\-width\fR / \fB\-height\fR default to \fB0\fR, meaning the size is computed from the content. Pass explicit values to override.
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
sequenceDiagram
  participant A            |  participant A as Alias  |  actor A
  autonumber
  A->>B: message
  activate A / deactivate A
  Note left of A: text  |  Note right of A: text  |  Note over A,B: text
  loop / opt / alt(+else) / par(+and) / critical / break / rect
    ...
  end
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBParticipants\fR are declared with \fBparticipant\fR/\fBactor\fR (optionally \fB... as Alias\fR) or created implicitly on first use in a message. They render in declaration order.
.IP \(bu
\fBArrows\fR: \fB\->\fR \fB\-\->\fR \fB\->>\fR \fB\-\->>\fR \fB\-x\fR \fB\-\-x\fR \fB\-)\fR \fB\-\-)\fR. One dash = solid, two = dotted; \fB>>\fR = filled head, \fB>\fR/\fB)\fR = open head, \fBx\fR = cross.
.IP \(bu
\fBSelf\-messages\fR (\fBA\->>A: ...\fR) draw as a loop on the lifeline.
.IP \(bu
\fBActivations\fR: \fBactivate\fR/\fBdeactivate\fR, or the shorthand \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR on a message arrow (\fBA\->>+B\fR activates B, \fBB\-\->>\-A\fR deactivates B).
.IP \(bu
\fBNotes\fR: \fBleft of\fR / \fBright of\fR / \fBover\fR one or two participants.
.IP \(bu
\fBautonumber\fR prefixes each message with a sequence number.
.IP \(bu
\fBFragments\fR \fBloop\fR \fBopt\fR \fBalt\fR(+\fBelse\fR) \fBpar\fR(+\fBand\fR) \fBcritical\fR \fBbreak\fR \fBrect\fR render as labelled, nestable frames; comments start with \fB%%\fR.
.SS "v1 scope"
.PP
\fBactor\fR is drawn as a box (no stick figure). Fragment frames span the full width and are indented per nesting depth, rather than enclosing only the involved lifelines. Not in v1: create/destroy of participants, \fBbox\fR grouping, and actor links/popups.
.SS Options
.PP
\fB\-fontfile\fR (a TTF for real\-font labels via \fBGlyphs\fR; PNG only \-\- otherwise the built\-in bitmap font), \fB\-scale\fR (positive integer; enlarges the PNG canvas, SVG ignores it).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tusequence
set src {sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor C as Client
  participant S as Server
  participant DB as Database
  C->>+S: Login (user, pass)
  S->>+DB: Select user
  Note over DB: hash not stored raw
  DB-->>-S: Salt & Hash
  alt Hash matches
    S-->>C: 200 OK & JWT
  else Wrong password
    S-->>-C: 401 Unauthorized
  end}
::tclutils::tusequence::writePng [::tclutils::tusequence::parse $src] login.png -scale 2
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR (canvas), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.IP \(bu
All shapes use rect / line / polygon primitives, so SVG and PNG output stay congruent.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUSEQUENCE <REASON>}\fR \-\- \fBEMPTY\fR (no participants), \fBARG\fR (bad \fB\-scale\fR), \fBFONT\fR (font file not found).
